    "$comment": "SHARED provider-routing corpus \u2014 the cross-language drift gate for model routing (rust/smooth-operator-core/src/providers.rs), per-model wire quirks (quirks.rs), and LiteLLM alias resolution (resolution.rs), plus their Go/TypeScript/Python/.NET ports. Every engine loads THIS file and asserts its own registry, quirk table and URL/parse helpers produce exactly these values. The expectations were GENERATED from the Rust reference, which is normative: if a port disagrees, the port is wrong. Routing is where a silent divergence is most expensive \u2014 a slot that resolves to the wrong model or the wrong base URL sends real traffic and real money somewhere nobody intended, and it looks like it is working. Presets are dumped with apiKey='test-key' and with SMOOAI_GATEWAY_URL unset, so the smooai-gateway rows pin the production default URL.",
